// A #buffer inside a module gets its own storage per instance, like every
// other member. The per-object setup simply had no case for DECL_BUFFER: it
// parsed fine and was then never allocated, and a member bound to it aliased
// an uninitialised view.
//
// Both branches of the parent lookup are exercised:
//   lo/hi  -> bound to B, a member of the SAME module  => per instance
//   gb     -> bound to Shared, a global buffer         => one for everyone
#buffer Shared:16

#module M
  #buffer B:16
  #variable lo:8 bind B[0..7]
  #variable hi:8 bind B[8..15]
  #variable gb:8 bind Shared[0..7]
  #variable whole = 0
  whole = B ? 1
#end

#M m1 lo=1 hi=2
#M m2 lo=9 hi=8

// Written through m2's view of the global; both instances must see it.
#variable seen1 = 0
#variable seen2 = 0
seen1 = m1.gb ? 1
seen2 = m2.gb ? 1
Shared = 4660 ? 1        // 0x1234, low byte 0x34 = 52
